nReason: I choose **B: f1-c4** because:\n1. It develops a piece with tempo, targeting the weak f7 square\n2. It prepares castling kingside for safety\n3. It's a flexible move that works well in many opening systems (Italian Game setup)\n4. The bishop is more active on c4 than it would be on other squares\n5. It maintains the option to castle and push d2-d4 next\n\nAnswer: B: f1-c4"}
