----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: a2-a4, P: a2-a3, N: b1-a3, N: b1-c3, P: b2-b4, P: b2-b3, P: c2-c3, P: d2-d4, P: d2-d3, R: f1-e1, R: f1-d1, P: f2-f4, P: f2-f3, K: g1-h1, P: g2-g4, P: g2-g3, P: h2-h4, P: h2-h3, Q: h5-g4, Q: h5-f3, Q: h5-e2, Q: h5-d1, Q: h5-g5, Q: h5-g6, Q: h5-f7, Q: h5-h4, Q: h5-h3, Q: h5-h6, Q: h5-h7]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Evaluation: Let me analyze the current position. I'm White and have my Queen aggressively positioned on h5. Looking at the board:\n\n1. **Q: h5-f7+** - This would be checkmate! The Queen on f7 would attack the Black King on e8. Let me verify:\n   - The King on e8 cannot capture the Queen on f7 (protected by nothing, but let me check escape squares)\n   - The King cannot move to d8 (controlled by Queen on f7)\n   - The King cannot move to d7 (controlled by Queen on f7)\n   - The King cannot move to e7 (controlled by Queen on f7)\n   - The King cannot move to f8 (controlled by Queen on f7)\n   - The King cannot move to f7 (occupied by Queen)\n   - No Black piece can capture the Queen on f7\n   - No Black piece can block\n   \n   Wait, let me reconsider - can any piece capture on f7? The Black King is on e8, and there's a pawn on e7. Actually, looking again at the board, e7 has a pawn (PBF0), so the Queen cannot go to f7 directly.\n\n2. **Q: h5-h7** - Attacks the pawn on h7, threatening the back rank\n3. **Q: h5-h8+** - Not in the list, but would be check\n4. **Q: h5-f7** - Actually this IS in my valid move list, which means f7 must be empty or the move is legal. Looking at row 7: PBF0 is at e7, f7 has PBF0... wait, the board shows f7 has PBF0.\n\nLet me re-read the position more carefully. If Q: h5-f7 is in my valid moves, it must be legal. This would give check to the King on e8, and if the King cannot escape and no piece can interpose or capture the Queen, it's checkmate.\n\nChecking if Black can respond to Qf7+:\n- King cannot move (all squares controlled or occupied)\n- Pawn on e7 cannot block\n- No piece can capture on f7\n\nThis appears to be checkmate!\n\nReason: Q: h5-f7 delivers checkmate. The Queen attacks the King on e8 from f7, and the Black King has no escape squares (d8, d7, e7, f8, f7 all controlled by the Queen or blocked), and no Black piece can capture the Queen or block the check.\n\nAnswer: Q: h5-f7"}
