ately challenges Black's advanced c4 pawn, fights for central control, and opens lines for developing my light-squared bishop (once I have one on c1 or if it develops). This move follows the principle of controlling the center and not allowing Black to maintain their space advantage for free. After Black captures cxd4, I can recapture and have equal central control.\n\nAnswer: P: d2-d4"}
